  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/cyclocheilichthys_janthochir_en/",
      "html": "<p>Cyclocheilichthys janthochir belongs to the barb family. Species of several barb genera with a similar body shape are commonly called \"shark\" in the hobby. In the fishhouse it got the nickname \"top-model-barb\", because it is very pretty but looks very skinny. It is neither fastidious regarding food, nor uptight in any other way.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/cyclocheilichthys_janthochir_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species originates from the island of Borneo.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/cyclocheilichthys_janthochir_en/",
      "html": "<p>It occurs in typical black water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/cyclocheilichthys_janthochir_en/",
      "html": "<p>Cyclocheilichthys janthochir is a schooling fish and certainly an enrichment for any large community tank.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/cyclocheilichthys_janthochir_en/",
      "html": "<p>The maximum size reported is around 20 cm. The specimens at the fishhouse are currently 5-7 cm long. With each centimetre the fish grow they become more beautiful, as the fins become more and more red.</p>"
    }
  ],
